{"name":"Nearsighted","hex":"#c8d5dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nearsighted","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of near-sighted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nearsighted"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myopia","blocks":[{"text":"Myopia, also known as nearsightedness or short-sightedness, is an eye condition where light from distant objects focuses in front of, instead of on, the retina. As a result, distant objects appear blurry, while close objects appear normal. Other symptoms may include headaches and eye strain. Severe myopia is associated with an increased risk of macular degeneration, retinal detachment, cataracts, and glaucoma."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Myopia_%28axial%29_diagram_NEI.jpg/330px-Myopia_%28axial%29_diagram_NEI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myopia","wikidata":"Q168403"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg/250px-Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg/250px-Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_with_myopia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_normal_vision_color_Hi-res.jpg/500px-Human_eyesight_two_children_and_ball_normal_visi